SUBTOPIC 7 - RESHAPE - CHANGE SHAPE
----------------------------------------------------
Explain:
Reshape = Change 1D to 2D, like Excel rows and columns. Data same, shape changes.

Where to use in Project?
You have 6 values, you want to show as table - 2 rows, 3 columns - Like Excel. Or you have image data, you need to reshape for model.

Old vs New - Advantage:
Old - List cannot reshape easily, need nested loops.
New - arr.reshape(2,3) - 1 line.

Example Code with Comment:
import numpy as np  # Import Numpy
arr = np.array([1000, 500, 2000, 3000, 4000, 6000])  # 1D - 6 values in 1 line
print(arr)  # Show 1D
arr_2d = arr.reshape(2, 3)  # 2 Rows, 3 Columns - Reshape
print(arr_2d)  # Show 2D
arr_3d = arr.reshape(3, 2)  # 3 Rows, 2 Columns - Reshape
print(arr_3d)  # Show 2D other shape

Input:
Array = [1000, 500, 2000, 3000, 4000, 6000]

Output:
[1000  500 2000 3000 4000 6000]
[[1000  500 2000]
 [3000 4000 6000]]
[[1000  500]
 [2000 3000]
 [4000 6000]]

Interview Question:
Q: What is reshape? Why use it?
A: Reshape changes shape without changing data. arr.reshape(2,3) makes 1D to 2D. In project, I use reshape to convert flat data to table format, and in ML, to convert image data to model input shape.

Project Code:
import numpy as np
data = np.array([1000, 500, 2000, 3000, 4000, 6000])  # Flat data
table = data.reshape(2, 3)  # 2 User groups, 3 values each
print(table)  # Show table

