SUBTOPIC 8 - BROADCASTING - SMALL + BIG
----------------------------------------------------
Explain:
Broadcasting = Small array + Big array, Numpy auto adjusts. Small value expands to match big array.

Where to use in Project?
Add same interest 100 to all users, or add different interest to different cities.

Old vs New - Advantage:
Old - Need loop to add same value to all.
New - Broadcasting - Numpy auto adds same value to all in 1 line.

Example Code with Comment:
import numpy as np  # Import Numpy
arr = np.array([[1000, 500], [2000, 3000]])  # 2x2 - 2 cities, 2 users
print(arr)  # Show original
print(arr + 100)  # Add 100 to all - Small value 100 broadcasts to all
print(arr + np.array([10, 20]))  # Add [10, 20] to each row - Broadcasting

Input:
Array = [[1000, 500], [2000, 3000]], Add = 100, Add Row = [10, 20]

Output:
[[1000  500]
 [2000 3000]]
[[1100  600]
 [2100 3100]]
[[1010  520]
 [2010 3020]]

Interview Question:
Q: What is Broadcasting in Numpy?
A: Broadcasting means Numpy automatically expands small array to match big array. Example - Array shape (2,2) + value 100 - Numpy adds 100 to all values. In project, I use this to add same interest to all users in 1 line.

Project Code:
import numpy as np
balances = np.array([[1000, 500], [2000, 3000]])  # 2 cities, 2 users
print(balances + 100)  # Add 100 interest to all - Broadcasting

