COMMON ERRORS IN NUMPY - IMPORTANT FOR UBUNTU
----------------------------------------------------
Error 1 - File name is numpy.py - WRONG
If you name your file numpy.py, Python imports your own file, not real Numpy.
Error: AttributeError: module 'numpy' has no attribute 'array'
Fix: Rename file - mv numpy.py my_numpy_test.py
And delete pycache - rm -rf __pycache__
Never name file as numpy.py, pandas.py, matplotlib.py. Use my_numpy_test.py, bank.py.

Error 2 - Pandas not installed
Error: ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'pandas'
Fix: pip3 install pandas
Check: python3 -c "import pandas; print(pandas.__version__)"

Error 3 - KeyError: 'bal2'
Error: KeyError: 'bal2' at df["bal3"] = df["bal2"] + 100
Meaning: DataFrame has column named balances, but you ask for bal2. Name mismatch.
Fix: Make name same everywhere. If DataFrame has bal2, use bal2. If DataFrame has balances, use balances.
Rule: np = Always Numpy, pd = Always Pandas. Never write import numpy as pd.

Error 4 - How to install Numpy in Ubuntu
Commands:
sudo apt update
sudo apt install python3 python3-pip -y
pip3 install numpy
python3 -c "import numpy; print('Numpy Installed')"
How to run command in Ubuntu: Press Ctrl + Alt + T to open Terminal, type command, press Enter.

